-- title:
--   Half-differences of dyadic means of smooth functions
-- statement:
--   For a sequence $u_k$ of smooth functions on a Hilbert space and the dyadic means $m_n(k)$ (averages of $2^n$ consecutive terms), the half block is
--   $$
--   \tfrac12\bigl(m_n(k)-m_n(k+2^n)\bigr).
--   $$
--
--   It is half the difference of two adjacent dyadic averages. These blocks are used to extract functions whose pairings with later molecules are small.
